[unipkg]: Run `unipkg` with no arguments to see version and command overview
[unipkg]: Use `unipkg launch-tui` for the interactive FZF-based package manager menu
[unipkg]: Run `unipkg generate` to auto-detect your installed managers and generate `unipkg.conf`
[unipkg]: Full system update: `unipkg update all && unipkg upgrade all`
[unipkg]: Browse available packages: `unipkg list available <index>` (e.g., `unipkg list available pacman`)
[unipkg]: Use `unipkg install all <package>` to try every configured manager until one succeeds
[unipkg]: Reorder managers in `~/.config/unipkg/unipkg.conf` — first entry is tried first
[unipkg]: Never run unipkg as root — it escalates via sudo internally
[unipkg]: Check installed packages: `unipkg list installed all`
[unipkg]: List configured managers: `unipkg indexes`
